      "## LSD And John Lilly",
      "Lilly's work became more controversial as he grew increasingly interested in LSD research.",
      "He administered LSD to some dolphins while studying their responses.",
      "The crucial distinction is Peter.",
      "Margaret opposed giving LSD to Peter and said Lilly agreed not to administer it to him.",
      "Therefore, the article should not say Peter was given LSD.",
      "Lilly's broader LSD work contributed to controversy around his scientific reputation and the laboratory's direction.",
      "The dolphin communication project had begun as an ambitious question about intelligence.",
      "By the mid-1960s, parts of the work were moving into territory that many scientists considered uncontrolled, unconventional and ethically troubling.",
      "## The Experiment Ends",
      "Funding eventually faded and Dolphin House closed.",
      "Peter and the other dolphins were transferred to Lilly's facility in Miami.",
      "The new environment was reportedly smaller and less stimulating than the flooded living space Peter had shared with Margaret.",
      "That move ended the central relationship on which the experiment had depended.",
      "It also revealed a weakness in the project design.",
      "When research becomes so dependent on one unusual environment and one human-animal bond, it becomes hard to reproduce, verify or continue elsewhere.",
